title: Reconcile rewritten branches
status: draft
created: 2026-11-22
author: Luke Carrier
approach: "Build the state machine and the Git refs first and wire them into the orchestrator second and add the host commands last. No requirement in the spec is marked `assumption`. The plan relies on facts the map already establishes. T-004 proves `git merge-tree --write-tree --merge-base` produces a usable tree and exit status. T-007 records the axes and the table. T-008 records the refs. Two implementation choices are settled here rather than deferred.\n\nThe observation rule. The classifier takes the workspace tree as an input and `plan` stays pure. The reconciler observes the workspace only when the plan can use the result: the branch tip differs from `synced` or `Merge` is `Pending` or the action is `Snapshot`. A read on a synced sandbox reads no workspace and returns `Proceed`. A mutating tool reads once after the tool. A branch that moved reads before the tool so the adoption is visible and again after it if the tool runs. That keeps one workspace read per tool call on the common path and two only when the branch moved. When the pre-plan defers the observation it passes `Clean`. The invariant is that the previous operation's post-plan snapshot left the sandbox at its own tip. A snapshot that fails returns an error and the next post-plan captures the work. Adoption is never reached without the observation because adoption needs a moved branch.\n\nThe snapshot split. `snapshot` commits on the sandbox branch and returns the revision. `advance` moves the shared branch. `set_synced` records the revision. A held branch takes the first write only. That is how a snapshot under `Pending` stays durable without moving the shared branch.\n\nFive steps. 1. Add `orchestrator/source.rs` with the axes and the plan and table tests. 2. Extend the contract and implement `synced` and `set_synced` and `set_tip` and the tree identity and the observation and the sandbox branch in `vcs::git`. 3. Add the ref helpers and the record field and the reconciler and wire it into create and exec and upload and download and snapshot and delete. 4. Add `vcs::git::reconcile` for the report and the staging worktree and finish and abort. 5. Add the CLI commands and the MCP tool and the tests.\n\nThe `git` binary. The host commands run `git` rather than `git2` because libgit2 cannot merge with an explicit base or write a conflicted working tree with markers. The binary is already required by the workflow the user finishes with. No crate is added."
architecture: "Four layers. `orchestrator/source.rs` is pure: it names no file and no ref and returns steps. `orchestrator/reconcile.rs` is the adapter: it reads the state through the contract and executes the steps. `vcs` is the contract and gains the tree identity and the observation and the host commands. `vcs::git` implements it and owns every ref write and every `git` invocation. The orchestrator names no backend and no ref string.\n\n{{mermaid: flow.mmd}}\n\nBoundaries. The new files sit inside existing arch-lint scopes so no rule changes. `orchestrator` still denies `vcs::git` and `vcs::git_common`. The CLI and MCP reach the host commands through the orchestrator. The pure plan depends on the contract only for `ConflictModel`.\n\nThe record. `StoredSandbox` gains an optional merge state. `Pending` is written when the plan blocks. The exit test is one ancestry check: the sandbox branch tip is an ancestor of the branch tip. That is the only ancestry test in the design and it never decides `Base` or `Workspace`.\n\nThe host workflow. Stage creates a linked worktree under the data directory on a temporary branch and merges with the recorded base. Resolve happens in the worktree with the user's editor. Finish moves the branch when it is free and prints `git merge --ff-only` when the user's checkout holds it. Abort removes the worktree and leaves the branch. Nothing writes the user's checkout."
technologies[5]{name,role}:
  "Rust 2024","The workspace language. No crate is added."
  "git2 0.21","Refs and trees and the observation and the compare-and-swap. Confined to `vcs::git` and `vcs::git_common`."
  "the git binary","The host commands run `worktree` and `merge-tree` and `read-tree` and `checkout --conflict` with hooks disabled. The workflow already requires it."
  "tar and tempfile","Staging directories and workspace materialisation."
  "arch-lint 0.11.0","The existing scopes cover the new files. No rule changes."
components[11]{name,purpose,details}:
  "orchestrator/source.rs","The axes and the classification and the plan. Pure and total.","Defines the three axes and `SourceState` and `Action` and `Step`. `classify` takes the two tips and the four trees and the recorded merge state. `plan` takes the state and the action and the conflict model and returns ordered steps. No I/O and no lock and no clock. A table test covers every combination. FR-001 to FR-004 and NFR-001."
  "vcs (contract)","Adds the facts and the host commands the orchestrator needs.","`src/vcs/mod.rs` and `types.rs` and `reconcile.rs`. `Vcs` gains `tree` and `sandbox_tip` and `set_sandbox_tip` and `advance` and `observe` and `is_ancestor` and `ensure_refs` and `report` and `stage` and `finish` and `discard_stage`. `synced` and `set_synced` and `set_tip` stop returning `Unsupported`. Neutral `Report` and `Staged` and `Finished` live in `vcs::reconcile`. The stub and `testing/vcs.rs` implement the new methods. Git leaves `merge` and `conflicts` and `resolve` and `abort` and `history` and `restore` unsupported. FR-018."
  "vcs::git refs","Creates and moves the three refs in the repository that holds the branch.","`src/vcs/git/refs.rs`. `branch_ref` and `sandbox_ref` and `synced_ref` resolve through `repo_for_branch`. `prepare` creates all three at the base. `delete_branch` removes all three. `ensure_refs` initialises the two bookkeeping refs from the branch tip when they are absent and logs it. `install_remote_in` adds `+refs/litterbox/workspaces/*:refs/remotes/litterbox/workspaces/*` to the exposed remote's fetch refspec. `open` sets `core.logAllRefUpdates=always` on the bare store. FR-011 and FR-012 and EC-001 and EC-012."
  "vcs::git identity and snapshot","Answers tree identity and splits the snapshot from the branch advance.","`src/vcs/git/scm.rs`. `tree` peels a revision to its root tree. `observe` builds a tree from the staged directory through `SnapshotFilter` with no commit. `sandbox_tip` reads the workspaces ref. `snapshot` commits the tree on the sandbox branch only. `advance` moves the shared branch. `set_synced` writes the synced ref. The compare-and-swap and the retry stay. `is_ancestor` uses a merge-base test. FR-002 and FR-003 and FR-009 and FR-013."
  "orchestrator/reconcile.rs","Observes and classifies and plans and executes at an operation boundary.","`state` calls `ensure_refs` and reads `synced` and the two tips and the record. `observe` downloads the workspace with the ignore selector and calls `Vcs::observe`. The pre-plan observes only when the branch moved or `Merge` is `Pending` or the action is `Snapshot`. `execute` runs `AdoptHistory` and `AdoptContent` and `Snapshot` and `Block` and `Proceed`. `AdoptContent` materialises the branch tip and uploads it over the workspace and deletes the paths the new tree lacks and reports the old sandbox tip when it is not an ancestor of the new tip. `Block` writes the record. The exit test clears `Pending` when the sandbox tip is an ancestor of the branch tip. FR-005 to FR-010 and FR-018."
  "orchestrator wiring","Runs reconciliation at every operation that touches the workspace.","`src/orchestrator/service.rs`. `create` uses the new `prepare` and writes no merge state. `exec` runs the pre-plan and the command and the post-plan. `upload` runs the pre-plan and the post-plan. `download` runs the pre-plan only. `snapshot` runs one plan with the `Snapshot` action. The MCP `write` tool drops its explicit snapshot because `upload` now snapshots. `delete` removes the refs and any staging worktree. `inspect` and `list` do not reconcile. `Performed` gains the post-plan state. FR-005 and FR-006 and FR-014."
  "vcs::git::reconcile","Reports and stages the host merge with the recorded base.","`src/vcs/git/reconcile.rs`. `report` runs `git merge-tree --write-tree --merge-base=<synced> <branch> <sandbox>` and parses the conflict paths. It names the branch reflog and the `git reflog show` command that lists the previous tips. `stage` creates `data_dir()/reconcile/<slug>/<sandbox>` with `git worktree add -b litterbox-reconcile/<name> <path> <branch tip>` then runs `git read-tree -m <synced> <branch> <sandbox>` and `git checkout --conflict=merge -- .` then writes `MERGE_HEAD` and `MERGE_MSG`. Every command runs with `-c core.hooksPath=<empty>`. `finish` checks a clean worktree and a descendant merge commit then moves the branch or prints the fast-forward command. `discard_stage` removes the worktree and deletes the temporary branch. FR-014 to FR-017 and NFR-005."
  "cli","The operator surface for the report and the workflow.","`src/cli.rs`. `status <name> [--json]` prints the report. `reconcile <name>` stages. `reconcile --finish <name>` finishes. `reconcile --abort <name>` discards. Each prints the worktree path and the conflict paths. FR-014 to FR-017."
  "mcp","One tool that stages and nothing else.","`src/mcp.rs`. `sandbox-reconcile` takes `{ sandbox }` and calls `stage`. It returns the worktree path and the conflict paths. It has no finish. The server registers it like the other tools. The harness's permissions decide whether an agent may call it. FR-016."
  "metadata_store","Persists the merge state.","`src/metadata_store.rs`. `StoredSandbox` gains `merge: Option<StoredMerge>` with `base` and `ours` and `theirs` as strings. `serde(default)` makes a legacy record read `None`. The field survives load and store round trips. FR-001 and FR-010 and EC-001."
  "tests","Proves the plan and the refs and the workflow.","`src/orchestrator/source.rs` has the plan table test. `src/vcs/git/vcs_tests.rs` covers ref initialisation and the snapshot split and the race. `src/vcs/git/reconcile_tests.rs` covers the report base and the markers and the index stages and `MERGE_HEAD` and the dirty refusal and the hook refusal and the missing refspec report and the second stage refusal and the stale worktree prune and the dirty checkout and the ignored file survival and finish and abort. Orchestrator tests use `TestVcs`. `metadata_store` tests cover the legacy record. AC-001 to AC-010 and EC-005 to EC-012."
dataFlow: "A tool call. `exec` or `upload` or `download` or `snapshot` takes the sandbox lock. The reconciler reads `synced` and the branch tip and the sandbox tip and the record. `classify` gives the state. When the branch moved or `Merge` is `Pending` the reconciler downloads the workspace and calls `observe` and plans. It runs the steps. `AdoptHistory` sets `synced`. `AdoptContent` replaces the workspace and moves the sandbox branch and `synced`. `Block` writes `Pending` and leaves the shared branch. Then the tool runs. The reconciler observes again and plans `Snapshot`. `snapshot` commits on the sandbox branch. When the branch is not held `advance` moves it and `set_synced` records the new revision. The result carries the state after the second plan.\n\nThe host workflow. `status` reads the two tips and `synced` and runs `merge-tree` with the recorded base. It writes no ref and no checkout file and it names the branch reflog that holds the previous tips. `reconcile` creates a linked worktree on a temporary branch at the branch tip and merges the sandbox branch with the recorded base. The user edits and commits. `reconcile --finish` moves the branch when it is free and prints the fast-forward command when the user's checkout holds it. `reconcile --abort` removes the worktree. The sandbox adopts at the next operation because the sandbox tip is an ancestor of the branch."
deployment: "No configuration key and no record migration. `prepare` sets `core.logAllRefUpdates=always` on the bare store so a dropped tip stays in the branch reflog. The CLI gains `status` and `reconcile` and the MCP server gains `sandbox-reconcile`. Land as five changes: the pure plan and its tests; the contract and the Git refs and identity; the reconciler and the wiring; the host commands; the CLI and MCP surfaces. Each change keeps the tree green because new trait methods ship with stub implementations and the Git implementation lands with its tests.\n\nGates: `cargo test -p agentkit-litterbox` and `cargo clippy -p agentkit-litterbox --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `arch-lint check` and `bash hack/arch-lint-negative.sh`. Smoke on a scratch repository under both `snapshot-mode` values: create a sandbox and snapshot once; rebase the branch and run a read and then a write and check adoption; edit the sandbox and rebase again and check `Pending`; run `status` and `reconcile`; resolve in the worktree and commit and finish; run another tool and check adoption. Under `remote` assert the refs live in the store and the fetch refspec carries the sandbox branch."
